    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. that's a good start. i've noticed that in some planning meetings, a lot of the pushback seems to come from people just being \"NIMBYs\"—you know, just trying to stop any change at all. how do you distinguish between legitimate infrastructure concerns and people who are just being irrational or selfish about their neighborhood character?",
