      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A key distinction to make is that legitimate infrastructure concerns usually focus on the tangible effects of a new development on daily life, such as increased traffic or strain on local services. In contrast, NIMBY concerns often center around the perceived loss of character, community, or identity that they feel would be harmed by the development. Assessing the facts and data can help you separate these two types of concerns, and demonstrate how the development can be designed and managed to mitigate its negative impacts.",
