      "role": "user",
      "content": "so you're saying the infrastructure stuff is \"tangible\" and the neighborhood character stuff is \"perceived\"? that feels like a pretty big distinction to make. it almost sounds like you're saying the character arguments aren't as valid because they're subjective. if i'm in this meeting, shouldn't i treat the \"loss of character\" concerns as serious points, or are they really just excuses for people to keep their property values high and keep neighbors out?",
